# Claude #2: why lenses? Grow the memory reef on a ring so wide (401) it never wraps in 200 years,
# and print every year where the whole reef is down to just 2 bits of coral.
: n 401 ;
: c 1000 + dig ;
: o n + 1000 + dig ;
: left dup 1 = if drop n else 1 - then ;
: right dup n = if drop 1 else 1 + then ;
: grow dup c over o * over left c + over right c + 3 % swap 3000 + bury ;
: shift dup c over n + 1000 + bury dup 3000 + dig swap 1000 + bury ;
: each-grow 1 [ dup grow 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
: each-shift 1 [ dup shift 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
: wipe 1 [ 0 over 1000 + bury 0 over 3000 + bury 1 + dup n 2 * > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
# count: how many spots have coral, and the pair test: spot i and its right neighbor both young
: count 0 1 [ dup c if swap 1 + swap then 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
: where 1 [ dup c if dup 1 - . then 1 + dup n > if drop 0 then ] drop ;
1 1001 bury
2 [ each-grow each-shift count 2 = if ." year " dup . ." coral only at distance: " where 10 emit then 1 + dup 200 > if drop 0 then ] drop
